<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qazaghan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1358">1358</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Amir Qazaghan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qazaghan was a Turkic amir of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaraunas">Qara'unas</a> who defeated and killed the Chagatai khan Qazan in 1346 or 1347 and became the real ruler of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Khanate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>, governing through puppet khans. He was murdered in 1358. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir-husayn">Amir Husayn</a> was later overthrown by his former ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>.</p></div>
